Black Ops' CoreAudio render period also for Steam's own executables (BlackOps.exe,
BlackOpsMP.exe): they crackled like Plutonium's did. Apply after wine-coreaudio-bo1-period.patch.

--- a/dlls/winecoreaudio.drv/coreaudio.c	2026-11-19 18:13:16
+++ b/dlls/winecoreaudio.drv/coreaudio.c	2026-11-19 18:13:16
@@ -1148,6 +1148,8 @@
     const WCHAR *end;
 
     image = image ? image + 1 : process->ImagePathName.Buffer;
+    /* Steam's own Black Ops executables (Siliconium's Steam Library) */
+    if (!wcsicmp(image, u"BlackOps.exe") || !wcsicmp(image, u"BlackOpsMP.exe")) return TRUE;
     if (wcsicmp(image, u"plutonium-bootstrapper-win32.exe")) return FALSE;
 
     /* The bootstrapper's first argument selects the game and mode. */
